.TH DB-HEALTH 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
db-health \- read-only connection and activity snapshot for SQL servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B db-health
.B --engine
.IR postgresql|mysql|mariadb
.RI [ --host " HOST" ]
.RI [ --port " PORT" ]
.RI [ --database " NAME" ]
.RI [ --user " NAME" ]
.RI [ --timeout " 1..30" ]
.RI [ --client " ABSOLUTE_PATH" ]
.RI [ --defaults-file " ABSOLUTE_PATH" ]
.RI [ --null ]
.br
.B db-health
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses a native client and a fixed, read-only SQL statement. Prints current
connections, active sessions/threads and server uptime. No SQL input or
passwords are accepted. This is a point-in-time metric snapshot, not a
health verdict. It must not be treated as a full lock or query audit.
.SH OUTPUT
Default fields are tab-separated ENGINE, SCOPE, CONNECTIONS, ACTIVE,
UPTIME_SECONDS. With
.B --null
exactly five NUL-delimited fields are emitted without a header. PostgreSQL
scope is cluster; MySQL and MariaDB scope is server.
.PP
MySQL/MariaDB report global Threads_connected, Threads_running and Uptime.
PostgreSQL counts client backends, client backends in active state, and
seconds since postmaster start. These are not identical activity semantics.
.SH PRIVILEGES
MySQL/MariaDB normally need only the ability to connect (USAGE).
PostgreSQL needs the effective pg_read_all_stats built-in role or superuser
for all sessions' state; insufficient rights produce exit code 1 and no
misleading partial report. This role can expose other sessions' SQL text.
.SH SECURITY
Explicit remote connections enforce certificate and hostname verification.
Without --host, MySQL/MariaDB use the local Unix socket. MySQL/MariaDB
--defaults-file must be a regular, private (0600), non-symlink file, with
approved [client] credential and TLS keys only. No included configuration,
startup SQL or arbitrary native switches are permitted. PostgreSQL uses
libpq credential mechanisms such as .pgpass or PGPASSFILE. Client output,
execution time and terminal output are bounded, and raw stderr is suppressed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: complete snapshot (not a health verdict).
.br
1: database connection/query failure or insufficient PostgreSQL statistics rights.
.br
2: invalid arguments.
.br
3: missing prerequisite, unsafe config, timeout or malformed client response.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR db-probe (1),
.BR psql (1),
.BR mysql (1),
.BR mariadb (1)
.SH DOCUMENTATION
See docs/commands/db-health.md and docs/commands/db-health.de.md.
